    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 3 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store numbers in E.164 form.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced the old \"strip to 10 digits\" logic with a new `toE164(...)` helper used on both create and update:\n- Strips spaces, dashes, and brackets.\n- If a leading `+` is present, keeps it and its country code as-is.\n- Otherwise assumes country code `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits.\n- Requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, throwing `InvalidTelephoneException` (\u2192 400) otherwise.\n- Duplicate detection now compares the stored E.164 strings directly (existing owners store E.164), instead of comparing digit-stripped values.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 Updated the entity validation from `@Digits`/`^[0-9]{10}$` to `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` so the persisted E.164 value validates, and removed the now-unused `@Digits` import.\n\n**Docs** \u2014 Updated `openapi.yml`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, and `DuplicateTelephoneException` Javadoc to describe the E.164 behavior.\n\nVerified against the acceptance tests: `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`, and `12` \u2192 400.",
